==Other methods==
===Level 35+: Tempoross===
{{Main|Tempoross}}
At level 35, players can challenge the Fishing boss, [[Tempoross]]. This method offers decent Fishing experience, [[Cooking]] experience, [[Construction]] experience, potential [[Strength]] experience, and rewards. When not cooking, Tempoross offers Fishing experience rates competitive with non-tick-manipulated [[Barbarian Fishing]].

Tempoross' [[reward pool]] can also be beneficial to low levelled players, possibly rewarding [[raw fish]], [[planks]], the [[fish barrel]] and [[tackle box]]. 

==== Solo Tempoross: 50,000 experience an hour ====
This method revolves around dealing 0 damage to Tempoross during his first attack phase and keeping his energy at 10% or below. 

The mechanics are predictable so each kill follows a repeating cycle:

* Fish 25-26
* Tether
* Dump all fish into the Ammunition crate
* Grab 5 buckets and fill them
* Clear fire (make sure to clear the fire on the boat before leaving)
* Drop buckets
* Fish 27
* Dump remaining fish
* Fish 27
* Dump 3 fish
* Attack Tempoross
* Dump remaining fish
* Colossal waves (Don't tether unless you still have fish while depositing)
* Fish 22-27 (This will vary depending on Tempoross's Essence but 24% should be low enough to deposit 27 fish)
* Dump remaining fish
* Kill Tempoross
* Grab bucket

Notes:

Prioritise leaping fishing spots.

The colossal wave special attack takes at least 6 seconds from the initial chat box message so don't be afraid to do actions in between before tethering. 

A charged Infernal Harpoon will '''not''' work with this method.

=== Level 65+: Karambwans ===
This gives up to 41,000 Fishing experience per hour and 150,000 banked Cooking experience per hour.

Requirements: Access to the [[fairy rings]] system. Completion of [[Tai Bwo Wannai Trio]] quest (note that the quest cannot be finished until you have 65 fishing if you burn the Karambwan given to you during the quest, as you'll need to catch and poison a replacement raw Karambwan for Ironmen). 

Recommended: [[Fish barrel]] for more AFK time. 

Travel to {{Fairycode|DKP}} with a fairy ring, fish an inventory full of karambwans, then bank them and return as quickly as you can. If you have a fairy ring in your [[player-owned house]], the fastest method is to deposit using your servant. If you're not accessing fairy rings using your POH (e.g. via a [[quest point cape]]) the closest deposit box is the gem mine, which requires [[Karamja gloves 3]]. Some players choose to bank via the fairy ring, but this method is slower than those listed above. The nearest fairy ring to bank is located by the [[Chasm of Fire]] ({{Fairycode|DJR}}). 

This method is very good when you need to AFK, but you're able to do something more click intensive than cutting [[Redwood tree|redwood trees]] or participating in the [[Nightmare Zone]].

Experience rates are shown below. These are somewhat pessimistic, as they do not assume [[Quest point cape]] for banking, nor the [[Fish barrel]] to cut down on banking times, nor the [[Angler's outfit]] for an extra 2.5% XP boost. With all additional items, it is possible to obtain as many as 875 karambwans per hour. 
